  "Diamond suggests that the chief \"lesson for the modern world\" in the history of the Fertile Crescent and China is that \"circumstances change, and past primacy is no guarantee of future primacy\" (417).",
  "You can modify a quotation, so long as you don't change its meaning and you signal deletions with three dots (called ellipses) and changes with square brackets.",
  "By this point you may be so sure that your evidence supports your reasons that you'll think readers can't miss its relevance.",
